1	# Local Server Setup
2	
3	This guide covers running the Shortcut MCP server locally using `npx`. This is the recommended approach for IDEs that don't yet support HTTP-based MCP servers, or if you prefer to self-host.
4	
5	All local configurations require a **Shortcut API token**. You can generate one at [https://app.shortcut.com/settings/account/api-tokens](https://app.shortcut.com/settings/account/api-tokens).
6	
7	> **Tip:** If your IDE supports HTTP-based MCP servers (like Cursor or VS Code), you can connect directly to `https://mcp.shortcut.com/mcp` instead — no API token or local setup required. See the [main README](../README.md) for details.
8	
9	## Windsurf
10	
11	See the [official Windsurf docs](https://docs.windsurf.com/windsurf/cascade/mcp) for more information.
12	
13	1. Open the `Windsurf MCP Configuration Panel`
14	2. Click `Add custom server`.
15	3. Add the following details and save the file:
16	
17	```json
18	{
19	  "mcpServers": {
20	    "shortcut": {
21	      "command": "npx",
22	      "args": [
23	        "-y",
24	        "@shortcut/mcp@latest"
25	      ],
26	      "env": {
27	        "SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN": "<YOUR_SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN>"
28	      }
29	    }
30	  }
31	}
32	```
33	
34	## Cursor
35	
36	[![Install MCP Server](https://cursor.com/deeplink/mcp-install-dark.svg)](https://cursor.com/en-US/install-mcp?name=shortcut&config=eyJlbnYiOnsiU0hPUlRDVVRfQVBJX1RPS0VOIjoiWU9VUl9UT0tFTiJ9LCJjb21tYW5kIjoibnB4IC15IEBzaG9ydGN1dC9tY3AifQ%3D%3D)
37	
38	See the [official Cursor docs](https://docs.cursor.com/context/model-context-protocol) for more information.
39	
40	1. Open (or create) the `mcp.json` file (it should be in `~/.cursor/mcp.json` or `<project-root>/.cursor/mcp.json`, but see Cursor docs for more details).
41	2. Add the following details and save the file:
42	
43	```json
44	{
45	  "mcpServers": {
46	    "shortcut": {
47	      "command": "npx",
48	      "args": [
49	        "-y",
50	        "@shortcut/mcp@latest"
51	      ],
52	      "env": {
53	        "SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN": "<YOUR_SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN>"
54	      }
55	    }
56	  }
57	}
58	```
59	
60	## Claude Code
61	
62	See the [official Claude Code docs](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/agents-and-tools/claude-code/tutorials#set-up-model-context-protocol-mcp) for more information.
63	
64	_You can add a new MCP server from the Claude Code CLI. But modifying the json file directly is simpler!_
65	
66	You can either add a new MCP server from the command line:
67	
68	```shell
69	# Grab your Shortcut token here: https://app.shortcut.com/settings/account/api-tokens
70	claude mcp add shortcut --transport=stdio -e SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN=$SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN -- npx -y @shortcut/mcp@latest
71	```
72	
73	Or you can edit the local JSON file directly:
74	
75	1. Open the Claude Code configuration file (it should be in `~/.claude.json`).
76	2. Find the `projects` > `mcpServers` section and add the following details and save the file:
77	
78	```json
79	{
80	  "projects": {
81	    "mcpServers": {
82	      "shortcut": {
83	        "command": "npx",
84	        "args": [
85	          "-y",
86	          "@shortcut/mcp@latest"
87	        ],
88	        "env": {
89	          "SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN": "<YOUR_SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN>"
90	        }
91	      }
92	    }
93	  }
94	}
95	```
96	
97	## Zed
98	
99	[Zed MCP Documentation](https://zed.dev/docs/ai/mcp)
100	1. Open your `settings.json` file. Instructions [here](https://zed.dev/docs/configuring-zed#settings-files)
101	2. Add the following details and save the file:
102	
103	```json
104	  "context_servers": {
105	    "shortcut": {
106	      "settings":{},
107	      "command": {
108	        "path": "<PATH/TO/NPX>",
109	        "args": [
110	          "-y",
111	          "@shortcut/mcp@latest"
112	        ],
113	        "env": {
114	          "SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN": "<YOUR_SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN>"
115	        }
116	      }
117	    }
118	  }
119	```
120	
121	## Common Issues
122	
123	### NPX command not working when using MISE for version management
124	
125	If you are using MISE for managing Node and NPM versions, you may encounter a "Client closed" error when trying to run the MCP server. Installing this extension into your IDE might help: https://github.com/hverlin/mise-vscode/.
126	
127	### MCP fails on startup in Gemini CLI
128	
129	If you are using the Gemini CLI and the MCP fails with the following error: `✕ Error during discovery for MCP server 'shortcut': MCP error -32000: Connection closed`, it might be due to an issue in Gemini where it redacts environment variables that contain the word `token`. You can either pass the Shortcut token as a CLI argument, or use the alternative name `SHORTCUT_API_TKN` instead of `SHORTCUT_API_TOKEN`. See the [Usage section](#usage) for more information.

